# Post-change build verification

After completing substantive code changes (not question-only or review-only turns):

1. Run `pnpm test:build` before telling the user the work is done.
2. If the build fails, fix the errors and run `pnpm test:build` again until it passes.
3. Do not ask the user to build manually when you can run the check yourself.

The project also has a Cursor **stop hook** (`.cursor/hooks.json`) that runs the same compile checks automatically after each agent turn. When build output appears as an auto follow-up message, treat it as a required fix before finishing.

Compile checks cover: `@blocks/core`, `@blocks/ui`, `web` (`next build`), and desktop (`tsc` + `vite build`). They intentionally skip electron installer packaging for speed.

Skip build verification only when the turn was read-only (no edits to `apps/`, `packages/`, or build scripts).
